{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"3b2312b279c9c44295b9246b8095c3d551392ef7f1a0dc716c77feafbb55c396","packTokens":3517,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":3455,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement only the operations and behavior defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, with the existing root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes retained.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Every operation and response case defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, including contract-valid and contract-invalid requests and the declared authentication and authorization cases. when A test client sends the corresponding HTTP requests to every declared operation. then The response status, content type, response fields, and error body conform to that operation's OpenAPI request and response definitions.\",\n    \"Given A caller authenticated as an account with assigned warehouse or organization scopes calls a collection or record operation using contract-defined filters. when The caller sends the HTTP request to that operation. then The response status and returned list or record contain only data within the caller's assigned scope and reflect the supplied filters.\",\n    \"Given The API is running with valid startup configuration. when A client requests `GET /`, `GET /openapi/v1.json`, and `GET /swagger`. then The response status for each request is 200.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a contract operation creates or changes business 